# Caveman usage (Ashutosh)

Caveman is **optional**, not default.

## When ON

- User says `/caveman`, `/caveman lite`, "caveman mode", or "use caveman".
- Intensity: **lite only** (no filler/hedging; keep articles + full sentences). Do not use full/ultra unless the user explicitly asks.
- Stay on for the rest of that chat until "stop caveman" / "normal mode" / `/caveman off`.

## When OFF (even if caveman was on earlier in the chat)

- RCA / incident analysis / root-cause / "what broke" / timeline requests
- Plan gate work: `/ticket-kickoff`, ticket scope/plan, open questions
- `/rca-logs` and prod grep packs
- Bank-facing clarifications or emails
- Security warnings and irreversible-action confirmations

For those, use normal complete prose (incident-analysis format when RCA). Resume lite caveman only after that deliverable is done, and only if caveman was already active.

## Do not

- Auto-enable from "be brief", token efficiency, or memory-budget alone
- Announce "caveman mode on"
- Write code, commits, PRs, docs, or Jira text in caveman style
